# CYBERDEMON — the Breachhead. A siege brute for the FPS roster: a heavy human
# chassis of meat and industrial prosthetics, built to close distance.
#
# AUTHORED FROM PROSE. There is no reference mesh and no reference plate for
# this character — by owner instruction, deliberately. So `blob:measure` and
# `blob:rings` do not apply (they exit 2 without a reference), and NO number
# below is "measured": every one is a design decision. The comment on each
# non-obvious number says WHY it is what it is, which is the house rule for a
# character with no mesh to fit against.
#
# WHO HE IS. The roster's heavy. The soldier is the ordinary grunt; this is
# what the grunt calls when a wall has to stop existing. He is not a monster
# species — he is a big man who has been rebuilt, and the rebuild is winning.
# The flesh that is left is the expensive part; everything that could be
# swapped for hydraulics has been.
#
# THE THREE BEATS that carry the silhouette (the brief's fixed four, made
# concrete):
#   1. THE RAM ARM. The left arm is gone above the elbow. In its place: a
#      shoulder cowl the size of a helmet, a hydraulic upper arm and a blocky
#      forearm ending in a blunt crusher head (all in cyberdemon-kit.wam).
#      It is heavier and longer than the flesh arm, so the figure reads
#      lopsided from every yaw — the ASYMMETRY is the silhouette.
#   2. THE LOOM. A bundle of exposed red cabling runs from the back power
#      unit, over the right shoulder, across the chest to the left socket.
#      Authored with `strand=` — the format's own bundle primitive — so it
#      reads as parallel conduits, a loom, not as veins.
#   3. THE SUNKEN HEAD. A small, forward-thrust skull with a heavy brow shelf,
#      tucked between the shoulder masses, with two lit optic eyes under the
#      shelf. A brute's head is SMALL on a brute's body; that ratio is the
#      read. Eyes are emissive PRIMS, not texture (the gargoyle road).
#
# NOT A MINOTAUR. No horns, no bovine muzzle, no hooves — the brief forbids
# the silhouette minotaur.blob already owns, and this file was written without
# opening it. The face is a blunt, flat-browed, short-muzzled brute face: an
# ape's, not a bull's. The mouth is the ONLY thing on the generated decal
# (make-cyberdemon-face.py); all other facial structure is prims.
#
# ASYMMETRY MAP: left arm replaced (flesh stump + kit), left leg sheathed in a
# load-bearing greave (kit over flesh), right arm and right leg bare flesh,
# skull plated on the left only. This file is flesh, stump, socket and the
# soft loom; the hard parts are characters/cyberdemon-kit.wam.
model cyberdemon
  # A head taller than the soldier (2.04) and a foot over the zombie (1.78):
  # the roster needs a body that reads "heavy" at arena distance, and height
  # is the cheapest way to say it. 2.15 also gives the kit's cowl room to sit
  # over the shoulder without swallowing the neck.
  height 2.15
  # Checked, not decorative — see blob-checks.ts. A coiled charge stance: the
  # knees fold FORWARD (humanoid), not back (digitigrade).
  stance humanoid

skeleton
  # Hip line at 1.12 (root 1.02 + len 0.10; children attach at the TAIL).
  # 0.52 of height — short legs, long torso and a heavy shoulder yoke is the
  # brute proportion; a 0.55+ hip line reads lanky, which is the opposite of
  # the brief. The pelvis LEN restores the crotch-to-hip-line segment the
  # WAM kit needs (WAM's root is a bare point; see goblin-kit.wam).
  root pelvis at 1.02 len=0.10

  # Hunched chain: the upper body leans FORWARD over the hips (pitch 10 then
  # 6, ~16 deg total) because the brief is "built to close distance" — a
  # charging posture, not a standing one. The neck pitches BACK (-8) so the
  # face still looks at the horizon instead of the floor, and the skull picks
  # up a small +4 so the crown sits level.
  bone spine parent=pelvis dir=up pitch=10 len=0.30
  bone chest parent=spine  dir=up pitch=6  len=0.30
  bone neck  parent=chest  dir=up pitch=-8 len=0.10
  bone skull parent=neck   dir=up pitch=4  len=0.24

  mirror
    # Shoulder socket at x ~0.245, y ~1.766 — just proud of the chest's
    # ~0.22 half-width (the goblin lesson: shoulder reach is a function of
    # chest width). tilt=12 lifts the clavicle so the yoke slopes up into the
    # neck like a brute's trap, not a coat hanger.
    bone clavicle parent=chest    dir=side tilt=12 len=0.26
    # Arms hang down and WELL out (tilt 16 then 6): a heavy body's arms cannot
    # hang flush or they meld into the lats, and this character is wider than
    # anything else in the cast. pitch 10/8 carries the hands forward of the
    # hips — the knuckles are ahead of the thighs, ready.
    bone upperArm parent=clavicle dir=down pitch=10 tilt=18 len=0.36
    bone foreArm  parent=upperArm dir=down pitch=8  tilt=6  len=0.34
    bone hand     parent=foreArm  dir=down pitch=4           len=0.13
    # Legs: thighs splayed to 0.115 (a heavy man stands wide), knee folds
    # forward 12 deg and the shin comes back -14 so the ankle lands under the
    # hip. Net knee offset from the hip->ankle line ~+0.11 m — a deep coil,
    # deliberately: this is the pose of someone about to lunge.
    bone thigh    parent=pelvis dir=down pitch=12 side=0.135 len=0.50
    bone shin     parent=thigh  dir=down pitch=-14          len=0.48
    # The foot bone only positions the foot prims (the house pattern).
    bone foot     parent=shin   dir=fwd                     len=0.17
  end

body
  # ============================================================
  # TORSO — four masses: haunch, waist, chest, trap yoke. Kept deliberately
  # NARROW in x (half-width ~0.22 at the chest) and deep instead: the goblin
  # paid twice for a wide torso whose arms then read as bulges, and this
  # character's arms are already further out than anyone's. Depth is where a
  # brute's mass lives anyway.
  # ============================================================
  # Haunch: the wide seat the legs root into. r 0.185 x wide 1.25 = 0.231
  # half-width, 0.20 half-depth — hips slightly narrower than the chest, so
  # the figure reads top-heavy.
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.30 r=0.195 wide=1.35 tall=1.05 deep=1.15 blend=0.016
  # Waist: cinched to 0.17 half-width so there is a break between haunch and
  # chest — without it the three masses blend into one barrel.
  blob torso on spine at=0.20 r=0.180 wide=1.15 tall=1.10 deep=1.10 blend=0.016
  # Chest: the biggest single mass, and the one the shoulders hang off.
  # r 0.185 x wide 1.20 = 0.222 half-width, deep 1.10 = 0.204.
  blob torso on chest at=0.50 r=0.195 wide=1.22 tall=1.15 deep=1.18 blend=0.016
  # Trap yoke: a shelf across the top of the chest, wide 2.0 so it reaches
  # past both shoulder sockets and the head can sink between them (the
  # gargoyle's traps idiom, which is what makes a small head read as small).
  blob torso on chest at=0.95 r=0.135 wide=1.75 tall=0.80 deep=1.00 blend=0.012
  # Pectorals: two slabs on the chest FRONT, offset forward and up. Without
  # them the chest is a barrel and the figure reads barrel-chested, not
  # slab-chested; `both` mirrors offset.x so one line makes the pair.
  blob torso on chest at=0.62 r=0.085 wide=1.25 deep=0.75 blend=0.010 offset=(0.080,0.010,0.120) both

  # ============================================================
  # NECK — thick column (r 0.088 against the zombie's 0.045). A brute has no
  # visible neck; this is the shortest, fattest one that still fuses head to
  # torso without the skull floating.
  # ============================================================
  bar head on neck from=0.05 to=0.95 r=0.088 deep=0.90 blend=0.008

  # ============================================================
  # RIGHT ARM — BARE FLESH. This is the "other side left as flesh" half of
  # the brief's asymmetry, so it is deliberately plain: deltoid, upper arm,
  # forearm, fist. No plates, no sleeve.
  # ============================================================
  # Deltoid: r 0.105 over a shoulder socket at x 0.245 — the cap sits proud
  # of the trap yoke so the joint reads from the front.
  blob arm on upperArm at=0.08 r=0.115 blend=0.012 side=r core
  bar  arm on upperArm from=0.14 to=0.92 r=0.100 r2=0.076 blend=0.008 side=r
  bar  arm on foreArm  from=0.06 to=0.94 r=0.090 r2=0.064 blend=0.008 side=r
  # Fist: a blunt block, slightly deeper than wide (a fist is). wide/tall 1.0
  # keeps it from reading as a paw.
  blob arm on hand at=0.55 r=0.085 wide=1.05 tall=0.95 deep=1.20 blend=0.010 side=r
  # Knuckle row: one bar across the front of the fist. `both` is unavailable
  # (this is one side), so the bar is centred and the fist's own width does
  # the splay.
  bar  arm on hand from=0.85 to=1.05 r=0.030 r2=0.022 blend=0.004 chamfer offset=(0,0.030,0.055) side=r

  # ============================================================
  # LEFT ARM — THE STUMP. The arm is amputated mid-upper-arm; everything
  # below the cut is the kit's hydraulic ram (cyberdemon-kit.wam). The stump
  # is authored to end at t~0.58 so the cowl has flesh to grip and the cut
  # face hides inside the shoulder housing. Deltoid matches the right side
  # exactly — the rebuild starts AT the socket, not at the shoulder.
  # ============================================================
  blob arm on upperArm at=0.08 r=0.115 blend=0.012 side=l core
  # The cut tapers slightly (r2 0.086) so the flesh looks pulled into the
  # socket rather than chopped square.
  bar  arm on upperArm from=0.14 to=0.58 r=0.100 r2=0.094 blend=0.008 side=l

  # ============================================================
  # LEGS — both flesh. The left is SHEATHED by the kit's greave, not replaced;
  # the brief asks for one limb replaced (the arm) and the asymmetry is
  # carried down the same side by the greave.
  # ============================================================
  # Thigh: r 0.125 x deep 1.05 — the heaviest limb segment, tapering to 0.085
  # at the knee so the joint stays slim.
  blob leg on thigh at=0.05 r=0.138 blend=0.012 mirror core
  bar  leg on thigh from=0.12 to=0.94 r=0.130 r2=0.092 deep=1.05 blend=0.012 mirror
  # Calf: a mass at the BACK of the shin (offset -z) — without it the shin is
  # a cone and the leg reads as a peg.
  # (to=1.05, not 0.90: the shin has to reach INTO the foot mass or the ankle
  # is a 9 mm air gap — strandedOf caught it at 9.3 mm on the first pass.)
  bar  leg on shin  from=0.05 to=1.05 r=0.105 r2=0.068 blend=0.010 mirror
  blob leg on shin  at=0.28 r=0.098 wide=1.00 tall=1.15 deep=0.85 blend=0.010 offset=(0,-0.010,-0.048) mirror
  # Foot: one long mass along the foot bone (deep 2.4 = 0.18 half-depth) so
  # the heel sits behind the ankle and the toe reaches past the toe joint.
  # offset y -0.095 drops it from the ankle (y 0.165) until the sole is on
  # the ground: 0.165 - 0.095 - (0.075 x tall 0.95) = 0.001.
  blob leg on foot at=0.35 r=0.082 wide=1.15 tall=0.95 deep=2.40 blend=0.012 offset=(0,-0.087,0) mirror
  # Toe cap: a squarer, slightly darker block at the front of the foot. Reads
  # as a booted toe on the flesh leg without being a kit part.
  bar  leg on foot from=0.62 to=1.02 r=0.068 r2=0.052 wide=1.05 tall=0.80 deep=1.00 blend=0.008 offset=(0,-0.087,0) mirror color=3a2f2c

  # ============================================================
  # THE LOOM — beat 2. Three `strand=` bundles (5 conduits each) run from
  # the back power unit, over the RIGHT shoulder, across the upper chest and
  # into the LEFT socket. They sit a centimetre proud of the skin: an exposed
  # conduit is strapped ON the body, and flush would read as paint.
  # `strand=` is the format's bundle primitive; using it here is the whole
  # reason the loom reads as a loom instead of as a fat vein.
  # ============================================================
  # Segment A — the CHEST BAND: a horizontal loom across the upper chest
  # from the left socket to the right shoulder. The curve bows FORWARD
  # (bend.z) to follow the pecs: measured torso front at y 1.68 is z 0.27,
  # so the chord midpoint at z 0.20 needs a 0.12 bow to land the bundle
  # centre just inside the skin (bundle reach ~0.047 m -> ~3 cm proud).
  bar torso on chest from=1.0 to=1.0 offset=(0.19,-0.034,0.117) tip=(-0.38,0,0) bend=(0,0,0.12) r=0.036 strand=4 wave=0.09 cycles=2 fat=0.85 blend=0.004 color=b81414 gloss=0.45
  # Segment B — over the RIGHT shoulder: from the band's right end, up over
  # the trap and down the back of the neck to the top of the back unit.
  bar torso on chest from=1.0 to=1.0 offset=(-0.19,-0.034,0.117) tip=(0.06,0.08,-0.22) bend=(0.01,0.03,0.03) r=0.034 strand=4 wave=0.09 cycles=2 fat=0.85 blend=0.004 color=b81414 gloss=0.45
  # Segment C — the BACK RUN: from the shoulder bundle down the right side of
  # the spine into the power unit. Measured back surface: z -0.13 at y 1.55
  # (x -0.12), z -0.11 at y 1.35 (x -0.06); the path rides just inside it.
  bar torso on spine from=1.0 to=1.0 offset=(-0.13,0.345,-0.072) tip=(0.07,-0.41,-0.09) bend=(0.02,-0.02,-0.05) r=0.034 strand=4 wave=0.09 cycles=2 fat=0.85 blend=0.004 color=b81414 gloss=0.45

  # ============================================================
  # HEAD — beat 3. All structure is PRIMS (the gargoyle road: no reference
  # mesh means blob:face-bake cannot run, and a fully painted face is the
  # documented failure mode). The face block below is shrunk to a NUB so it
  # emits nothing; the decal carries the mouth and nothing else.
  # The skull bone runs (0,1.813,0.070) -> (0,2.052,0.086); `at=` is a
  # fraction along it and `offset=` is a world displacement from that point.
  # ============================================================
  # Cranium: the dominant mass and deliberately the FATTEST unpainted head
  # prim, because lab-main's headShape() picks that one as the decal's hs
  # frame — pick it, do not leave it to chance (thornbeast lesson). r 0.135 x
  # tall 1.30 = 0.176 semi-height; centred y 1.976 so the crown lands on
  # 2.151, i.e. the declared height.
  blob head on skull at=0.68 r=0.135 wide=1.10 tall=1.30 deep=1.15 blend=0.006
  # Cheek/jaw mass: wide (1.60) and low, the jowls of a heavy man. r 0.092 x
  # wide 1.60 = 0.147 < the cranium's 0.176, so the hs frame stays the cranium.
  blob head on skull at=0.28 r=0.092 wide=1.60 tall=0.90 deep=1.10 blend=0.005 offset=(0,-0.040,0.045)
  # Brow shelf: TWO prims, asymmetric on purpose — the left (augmented) side
  # is heavier and squarer, the right side lighter. Both sit at y ~2.00, z
  # ~0.19, jutting past the cranium's front so the eye sockets are shadowed.
  blob head on skull at=0.62 r=0.058 wide=1.35 tall=0.62 deep=0.80 blend=0.004 offset=(0.075,0.042,0.112) color=4a3b3a
  blob head on skull at=0.62 r=0.050 wide=1.30 tall=0.55 deep=0.75 blend=0.004 offset=(-0.072,0.038,0.108) color=4a3b3a
  # Muzzle: SHORT and blunt (deep 1.25, not a bull's snout). Front at z 0.289
  # — it clears the brow so the mouth decal has a surface to land on, but
  # only by 6 cm, which keeps the mouth at |hs| ~1.6 (well inside the 1.95
  # decal fade the thornbeast paid for).
  blob head on skull at=0.40 r=0.062 wide=1.30 tall=0.85 deep=1.25 blend=0.005 offset=(0,-0.055,0.135)
  # Nose pad: a small blunt wedge between the brows. No bridge — a brute's
  # nose is a smear, not a beak.
  blob head on skull at=0.52 r=0.030 wide=1.10 tall=0.90 deep=1.00 blend=0.004 offset=(0,-0.005,0.175)
  # Jaw/chin: the mass under the mouth. r 0.072 x wide 1.35 = 0.097; bottom at
  # y 1.730, which is 7 cm below the cranium's bottom (1.800) — the heavy
  # under-jaw that makes the head read as a brute's, not a skull's.
  blob head on skull at=0.18 r=0.072 wide=1.35 tall=0.70 deep=1.15 blend=0.005 offset=(0,-0.075,0.085)
  # OPTIC EYES — the lit pair. Colour IS the emission (`glow=`), so these read
  # in a dim room with no light in the scene. Asymmetric by design: the left
  # optic is the replacement (bigger, a lens in a socket), the right is the
  # man's own eye (smaller). Both are painted, which also keeps them out of
  # the hs-frame pick.
  blob head on skull at=0.60 r=0.024 blend=0.003 chamfer offset=(0.058,0.020,0.150) tip=(0.006,0.004,0.030) color=8fe6ff glow=1.0
  blob head on skull at=0.60 r=0.018 blend=0.003 chamfer offset=(-0.058,0.020,0.150) tip=(-0.005,0.003,0.026) color=8fe6ff glow=1.0

# ============================================================
# FACE DECAL — the mouth and NOTHING else. There is no reference mesh, so
# blob:face-bake cannot run; the gargoyle is the precedent for a mesh-less
# face (all structure is prims, the decal carries the mouth). The PNG is
# generated by scripts/make-cyberdemon-face.py, which is committed beside it —
# the gargoyle's has no generator and cannot be regenerated without redrawing
# it by hand.
#
# The sheet's own GLOW is gated OFF (eyeGlowCut 0.99, eyeGlowAmp 0): the
# gargoyle's near-white teeth cleared the default cut and rendered as glowing
# red fangs, and the all-white-sheet-glows-red trap is one of the two this
# project already paid for. The eyes are emissive PRIMS and need no help.
#
# projScale is a FREQUENCY (lower = bigger), and the numbers below are solved
# against the cranium hs frame printed by the checker:
#   cranium centre (0, 1.976, 0.081), axes (0.149, 0.176, 0.155).
#   Mouth target: world (0, 1.840, 0.289) -> hs (0.00, -0.77, 1.35).
#   The image draws the mouth centred at uv (0.50, 0.50), so
#   centreY = 0.50 - (-0.77 x scaleY) and centreX = 0.50.
# scaleX/scaleY 0.30 make the mouth ~0.36 of the texture wide, which is the
# fraction the script draws.
# ============================================================
sheet
  image       cyberdemon-face.png
  decal       0
  projScaleX  0.30
  projScaleY  0.30
  projCentreX 0.50
  projCentreY 0.73
  eyeGlowCut  0.99
  eyeGlowAmp  0

# Face block: SHRUNK TO A NUB. headRadius 0.001 kills the emitted skull
# ellipsoid pair; browHeavy/noseLength 0 gate the emitted brow and nose off
# (facePrims emits only while those are > 0.0005). The head above is authored
# prims; this keeps the block present (and the lab's face panel live) without
# imposing the house oval. Same trick as gargoyle.blob.
face
  headRadius 0.001
  headWidth  1.0
  headHeight 1.0
  headDepth  1.0
  jawWidth   1.0
  jawHeight  1.0
  jawDrop    0
  jawJut     0
  noseLength 0
  noseWidth  1.0
  noseDrop   0
  browHeavy  0
  browRise   0
  headBlend  0.006

# Ash-grey mauve flesh: a man who has not seen sun in a long time, with the
# grime of the rebuild in it. Linear values; the shader sRGB-encodes, which
# lifts the low channels hard, so the numbers are darker than they read.
# baseColor 0.30/0.16/0.14 is a desaturated maroon-grey — NOT the zombie's
# pink and not the gargoyle's blue stone. mottleColor is COOL (0.10/0.12/0.16)
# so the variation reads as dirt ON the body rather than darker meat IN it
# (the mottle-hue rule in the palette reference). Wound interior stays red.
palette
  baseColor     0.320 0.200 0.185
  deepColor     0.500 0.080 0.080
  charColor     0.090 0.070 0.070
  specIntensity 0.50
  specRoughness 0.42
  fresnelBoost  0.35
  translucency  0.08
  wetness       0.18
  surfaceNoiseAmp    0.06
  silhouetteNoiseAmp 0.02
  mottleAmp     0.45
  mottleScale   2.0
  mottleColor   0.080 0.100 0.140
